# Atomic composition (molecules compose atoms)

When **building or editing** WMDS components in `src/components/molecules/` or `organisms/`:

## Rule

Every **visual affordance** inside a molecule must come from an **existing atom** (or an atom extended with a documented pattern). The molecule owns **shell, layout, state, and composition** — not duplicate mini-atoms.

| Affordance | Compose from | Not this |
|------------|--------------|----------|
| Icon-only action (×, kebab, edit) | **`IconButton`** (`inset` for chip innards) | Raw `<button>` + Lucide + local classes |
| Leading Lucide glyph | **`ButtonIcon`** / **`BadgeIcon`** | Molecule-local `*Icon.tsx` wrappers |
| Status / category label | **`Badge`** (`emphasis="muted"` for soft copy) | Hand-rolled pill spans |
| Outcome mark (✓ / × circle) | **`Badge iconOnly`** | Custom filled circles in molecules |
| Segment / filter count | **`BadgeSegmentCount`** | `CountPill` or inline count spans in `lib/` |
| Text field | **`Input`** / **`TextArea`** | Custom input shells |
| Primary/secondary action | **`Button`** | Styled `<button>` with `bg-primary` |
| Detail / settings row | **`Button layout="row"`** | Raw flat `<button>` rows |
| Loading spinner in control | **`ButtonSpinner`** | Ad-hoc SVG/CSS spinners |
| 8px semantic dot | **`Status variant="dot"`** | Custom dots |
| Task progress ring (24px) | **`Status variant="ring"`** | Inline SVG rings in molecules |

## When sizing doesn't fit

**Extend the atom** (new size, `inset` pattern, Storybook spec) — then compose it. Do **not** fork a one-off inside the molecule.

Example: removable **Chip** dismiss → `IconButton inset`, not `chipRemoveButtonClasses`.

## Allowed in molecules

- `*Styles.ts` for the **molecule shell** (Card gutter, Chip filter toggle, TaskRows row chrome)
- Context providers (`ChipFilterGroup`), compound slots documented in Storybook
- **`lib/`** helpers that are **not** visual affordances (motion, cn, typography maps)
- Composing other **molecules** when documented (TaskRows + Chip, Search + Button + Input; **TaskRows** composes **Accordion**)

## Before finishing a molecule PR

1. Grep the molecule folder for raw `<button`, local `*Icon.tsx`, and affordance-like class blocks in the TSX (not `*Styles.ts` shell).
2. Map each piece to an atom or a documented exception in the story **Anatomy**.
3. If you added a new atom pattern, add or update the atom Storybook story first.
4. Header / filter / toolbar rows — pick a **cluster tier** (Foundation → Cluster) and pair Chip + IconButton + Button sizes from the canonical table.
5. Run **`npm run validate:composition`** — **`openGaps`** and **`compositionTrackedOpenGaps`** must stay empty. Documented shells only in **`compositionShellExceptions`** (Accordion, Chip, etc.).

See **`AGENTS.md` → Molecule composition** and **ADR-0002**, **ADR-0011**.
